{sov: Notes}
Signature Riff: Built around the iconic repeating bass and guitar line in G
Pentatonic / G Mixolydian, punctuated by the cowbell backbeat.

Chord Syncopation: The change to C7 hits as a fast upbeat stab on the 'and' of
beat 2, resolving immediately back to G7 on beat 3.

Rhythm Guitar: Play light, muted 16th-note chucks with short, staccato G9 and
C9 voicings on the top strings to leave room for the bassline.

Arrangement: The entire track loops this 2-bar groove framework for the
verses, harmonica solos, and sax breakdown.
{eov}